OL,3,GNEWSAMemorial service held for 'titan
OL,4,Aof industry' Sir Ian Wood
OL,5,
OL,6,FTributes have been paid to the
OL,7,FAberdeen-based businessman and
OL,8,Fphilanthropist Sir Ian Wood at a
OL,9,Fmemorial service, following his death
OL,10,Fin July at the age of 84.
OL,12,FSir Ian was one of the UK oil and gas
OL,13,Findustry's most respected leaders, who
OL,14,Fturned his family's fishing boat repair
OL,15,Fyard into a global engineering giant.
OL,17,FAt its height, the Wood Group was
OL,18,Fvalued at more than #5bn, carrying out
OL,19,Fwork around the world in the energy
OL,20,Fsector.
